
-don't do default event from HTML elements
-don't add events in the HTML file, always in JS, this mixes the two files and makes things confusing
-there are several different types of events
-don't do keypress and keydown at the same time it will prob crash

-Every event has a target (usually what has the .eventlistener(type, function) added to it)
-you could do .onclick in js but it is not recommended
-with addEventListener(), you can add more than 1 event to 1 target, with other methods this isn't possible


mouseover/mouseout are mouseenter/mouseleave
k_event.Key is e.Key (it still needs to be a parameter in the function)
.preventDefault() prevents the default action of the key, for example it prevents a new line from
being created via the enter button




